WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.190
What should school districts tell
families after a capital project is

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:07.950
funded? Start with three things: what
has been approved, what families

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:11.330
can still influence, and when they will
hear from you again.

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:15.710
A funded project still needs a
school-by-school communication plan.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.930
Imagine construction will move a
school's entrance.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:23.850
Share a dated map with the new route,
the start date, and who families can

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:28.570
contact. Ask which parts of the plan are
difficult for people using the bus,

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:31.970
walking to school, or using accessible
parking.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:34.650
Offer more than one way to respond.

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:37.490
A campus forum can surface questions
quickly.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:41.970
A written follow-up gives families who
cannot attend a chance to weigh in.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:47.210
Then report back: what changed, what is
still open, and when

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:48.910
you will share the next update.

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:53.830
On Montgomery Public Schools' capital
program, PRC Impact supported

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:58.190
community forums and public
communications as a subconsultant to
Volkert.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:01.590
Use the campus checklist to plan your
next update.

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:06.070
If your district wants help planning
community engagement, start a project

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:08.230
at prcimpact.com.
